    "nts2": [
      {
        "n": "HEARING VOICES W/ SANDRO MARAVILLAS",
        "s": "2026-10-05T08:00:00+01:00",
        "e": "2026-10-05T09:00:00+01:00",
        "d": "“El Bailable”, that Latin American institution. Glorious deed of New Year’s Eve, expressive national celebration and infamous baptisms. Bursting with mischief lyrics, \"letras picaronas\", it’s a joy in and of itself, like a juicy ceviche. “Yet another year gone? Who cares” sang Tommy Rey, indifferent to the feeling of getting older. From my early memories of flawed adults having massive fun in Chile, to contemporary iterations of the big styles, these songs are a celebratory journey across the diversity of Latin-American rhythms.",
        "j": null,
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/dancing-2026/episodes/dancing-2026-hearing-voices-w-sandro-maravillas-5th-october-2026"
      },
      {
        "n": "BABY'S WAY W/ MAMMY FINGERS",
        "s": "2026-10-05T09:00:00+01:00",
        "e": "2026-10-05T10:00:00+01:00",
        "d": "When babies are born they enter into a dyad with their caregiver, usually their mother. Their deepest thoughts, experiences, and intentions are revealed through the language of their bodies in active dialogue. The intricate rhythms of their movements, the timing of their gestures, and the spatial shifts of posture comprise their unique choreography in the dance of relating. This is mother and baby’s way… \nInspired by my experience of observing a mother-infant relationship, this lighthearted mix puts music to some of the non-verbal cues, embodied attunement, and playful reciprocity that lie at the heart of this most primal dance!",
        "j": null,
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/dancing-2026/episodes/dancing-2026-baby-s-way-w-mammy-fingers-5th-october-2026"
